<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saxe-Weissenfels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1656">1656</a>–<a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weissenfels">Weissenfels</a> was a duchy created in 1656–1657 for Augustus, a younger son of Elector John George I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, with its residence at Weissenfels on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> from 1680. Its court was noted for music, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-sebastian-bach">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> held the honorary title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapellmeister">Kapellmeister</a> to the duke. When the line died out in 1746, its lands returned to the Electorate of Saxony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saxe-weissenfels.jpg" alt="Saxe-Weissenfels" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Concord · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Neu-Augustusburg_Ostseite.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
